.TH PREGO 1 "2026" "prego3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
prego \- system test framework based on Python3 test cases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prego
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPYTEST\-ARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B prego
is a Python3 library and pytest plugin consisting of a set of classes and
hamcrest matchers useful to specify shell command interactions through
files, environment variables and network ports. It provides support to
run shell commands in the background, send signals to processes, and set
assertions on command stdout or stderr, among other things.
.PP
The
.B prego
command runs the test suite in the current directory using pytest,
with a reporter tailored to prego test cases. Any trailing arguments are
passed through to pytest.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
explicit config file
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep\-going
continue even with failed assertion or tests
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dirty
do not remove generated files
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-stdout
print tests stdout
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-stderr
print tests stderr
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-time\-tag
include time info in logs
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
increase log verbosity (repeatable)
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-plain
avoid colors and styling in output
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pytest (1)
